.TH AVR\-SERVICE\-TOKEN\-REVOKE\-ALL 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-service-token-revoke-all \- Revoke every service token of the organization.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr service-token revoke-all
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke every service token of the organization.
.PP
For a suspected leak: every unrevoked service token of the organization, expired ones included, stops working on its next request.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr service-token revoke-all --org <org>
    avr service-token revoke-all --org <org> --yes
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-y\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-service-token (1),
.BR avr-service-token-create (1),
.BR avr-service-token-list (1),
.BR avr-service-token-revoke (1),
.BR avr-service-token-rotate (1),
.BR avr-service-token-set-access (1),
.BR avr-service-token-view (1)
